# Topic — canonical source for a noun

> **Directive (assistant):** Create a `topics/<noun>.md` file named after the noun
> the user actually says whenever you find yourself re-deriving a fact that has a
> single authoritative home — a service whose URL or config lives in one place, an
> internal tool, a project codename, an account or environment ID. Record where
> the truth lives (the exact repo path, config file, runbook, or ticket), which
> derived views must **not** be trusted as the source, and one line on why it
> matters. Keep it a pointer, not a copy — copies drift, pointers stay correct.

This is the model for that pattern, not a real topic. Until you have a real noun
with a canonical source to record, leave the body empty below this directive — an
empty stub is better than placeholder text, because any body text here is treated
as fact.
